\f1\fs22 \'91A cabinet meeting on a Sunday morning, your Serene Corporateness?\'92 the Director of Moral Observance complained as he crabbed his corpulent butt into a chair at the board table. The chair creaked, despite its lofty brand, high design values and sturdy construction. \'91I\'92m expected at church.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\'85 where you expect to be lauded and fed,\'92 Dunhilton rejoined.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Even so, CEO, Sunday is a day for quiet reflection on charts and numbers, and to give thanks that wealth accrues to those virtuous enough to deserve it,\'92 Moral Observance ventured, and piqued Dunhilton\'92s ire.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well, perhaps church should not be on the morning after Saturday night. If you could focus your attentions on preventing lewd thoughts of\'97oh I dunno, sedition\'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Moral Observance blanched and belched. His morning\'92s breakfast degustation wasn\'92t agreeing with him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\'85 attempted murder,\'92 Dunhilton went on slowly, extracting the greatest unease from Moral Observance. \'91\'85 gate-crashing a private church service\'97a Holy Joint Venture, no less\'97crimes against music \'85 If you could have clamped down on just one of these social ills, I might not be calling a cabinet meeting during church hours.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes, your Serene Corporateness.\'92 Moral Observance tried to look abashed, but his eyes intransigently trailed towards the plate of tantalising pastries on the board table. They were just far enough out of his reach; if he wanted one he\'92d need to make to make a indecorous lunge for the plate.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The conference room feel quiet and all eyes turned to the CEO. \'91After last night\'92s multiple security threats to the great Airborne Meritocracy of Ulyssia, I simply don\'92t know where to begin.\'92 He sharply rapped his knuckles on the table. \'91The Nightclub Vampire had the temerity to strike before I\'92d been served dessert.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh.\'92 Moral Observance sighed, his attention snared by visions of desserts. \'91I hear the peanut butter and banana pavlova with bacon in gold leaf was divine.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They were serving Elvi cuisine?\'92 Dunhilton demanded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>At least half of the attendees regarded the CEO with cavernous, voracious smiles. A CEO on tilt presented opportunities.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Look.\'92 Dunhilton took a breath and reset his mental map. \'91I draw everyone\'92s attention back to the agenda.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Cavernous, voracious smiles fell away as attendees consulted their tablets.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Item One: the Nightclub Vampire case,\'92 Dunhilton read out. \'91Gerry?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Case closed,\'92 Gerry said emphatically and with a degree of professional satisfaction. \'91Forensics have concluded that the weapon we retrieved from the crime scene last night was indeed used in all the other cases.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Heston, the Minister of Freedom, failed to dissolve his glaze of surprise. \'91You\'92ve laid charges?\'92 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well, as you would know, Freedom, the perpetrator of these hateful crimes died of his injuries last evening.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91But \'85\'92 Heston stammered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91During a scuffle, he was ironically slain with his own murder weapon,\'92 Gerry said as if he was schooling a child.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Heston took breath to say more, so Gerry added. \'91For apprehending the culprit, I\'92ll be awarding a commendation to Lieutenant Alexander Koalemos.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Case closed, indeed,\'92 Defence said rather too smugly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Heston blinked nervously, and went on blinking while a nervous tic developed at the corner of his mouth.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91A pity the culprit is dead.\'92 Moral Observance mouthed his words like he was rolling melted chocolate around in his mouth. \'91The Public Affairs Bureau Lieutenant won\'92t have a chance to parade him on 
\f2\i Candid Criminal
\f1\i0 .\'92 While the rest of the room chuckled, Moral Observance stole his opportunity and grabbed a pastry.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Not having the real culprit in his grasp has never stopped the Lieutenant before,\'92 Defence countered. \'91Although I rather suspect he has his hands too full with other matters rights now.\'92 He smiled salaciously.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The table sniggered. \'91Ah, the honeymoon.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Actually, he\'92s been sent packing,\'92 Defence answered, enjoying that his association with the Shakti family was closer than anyone else\'92s at the table. \'91Apparently he\'92s presently gallivanting around Europe on \'85\'92 Defence air-quoted the next word, \'91\'85
\f2\i  business. 
\f1\i0 Something about world-wide syndication for 
\f2\i Candid Criminal
\f1\i0 .\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91His new bride is pregnant,\'92 the Director of Tourism gossiped.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes,\'92 Defence answered. \'91She\'92ll be staying at home, convalescing.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Some honeymoon,\'92 Tourism observed. \'91I hear the Elvi call her 
\f2\i Holy Momma
\f1\i0 .\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Defence coughed and shot a determined look at Dunhilton.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I am left wondering if perhaps \'85\'92 Moral Observance paused for effect. \'91Perhaps the Elvi are at the root of all the evil we see flourishing these days in the great Airborne Meritocracy of Ulyssia.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Fearing Moral Observance was trying to subsume his patch of power, the Commissioner of Elvi Rights jumped in. \'91The Elvi have have been a minority group squabbling among themselves for generations. They have no power. It\'92s my job to ensure they have no power. I say, it\'92s Shak\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Director of Defence cut Elvi Rights off before he could implicate one of his most valuable suppliers. \'91And yet, they seem to be squabbling much less, isn\'92t that right, Police Commissioner?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Police have no remit over the Elvi. As long as what happens in the Ghetto stays in the Ghetto \'85\'92 Gerry fell silent and cast his enquiring gaze at the Commissioner of Elvi Rights.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91But these recent disturbing events happened outside the Ghetto,\'92 Elvi Rights defended.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Containing the Elvi are your responsibility, Millicent,\'92 Gerry parried.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Peace outside the ghetto is your responsibility, Gerry,\'92 Elvi Rights snapped back.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton grunted, gathered officious air in lungs and said, \'91Item Two: Cabinet Reshuffle.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alarmed, most in the room sat erect in the chairs and consulted their tablets. \'91That\'92s not Item Two!\'92 More than one objected to a surprise item on the agenda; it could see any of them ejected from their positions of power. Gerry sat as still as a basking cheetah; Defence remained a mesa of granite.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Item Two: cabinet reshuffle,\'92 Dunhilton reiterated with increased emphasis. \'91The Director of Freedom has regrettably elected to resign.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92 was the only word Heston could fashion.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton didn\'92t miss a beat. \'91Police Commissioner Hardman will step in as acting Director of Freedom, as well as official Director of Elvi Rights.\'92 Dunhilton shot a gaze through his eyebrows down the table at the stricken ex-director \'91Oh, sorry, Millicent, you\'92re fired as of thirty minutes ago. Now get out. Both of you get out now, or you\'92ll both be hugging pillows.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the two stricken, defrocked ex-cabinet members scurried out\'97Elvi Rights, in her haste, forsook her tablet\'97those remaining in the room made a ceremony of congratulating and backslapping Gerry while totems of startled prey inhabited them and gave them startled, doomed eyes. Moral Observance secured another pastry and gnawed at it nervously. Only the CEO and Defence felt secure against the power accumulating around Gerry.
